  i think we've got communities across  valley and spain  who um are sadly a bit disillusioned  with politics  and disillusioned with traditional sort  of politicians  one of the things i really want to focus  on is how we get people engaged with  politics in a positive way  and i think sometimes you know we've had  people come here this by-election with  their own agendas and their own egos  um and i've played into people's  frustrations  and my job now is to bring those people  together  around a shared vision for a prosperous  and bright future for valley and spain  he says he's going to contend the result  what you can test the result what do you  think  listen i'm focused on the rest of my day  which is celebrating with an amazing  team  who have supported me throughout this  campaign uh getting back in touch with  my family and friends who i've barely  seen during the last few weeks  um and then cracking on with the job of  being the mp for ballet and spain  yeah i mean he did take 22 percent of  the vote didn't he and that was on an  anti-labor stance it does look as though  uh much of the  muslim community as was uh supporting  him  rather than you what do you need to do  to bring them back into the fold  i've spent the last few years working  for the joe cox foundation uh building  communities across badly in spain and  indeed at a national level  um and i'll continue to do that and i  think sadly the divisive nature of  other people's campaigns um means that  that word  work still needs to be done but if  anyone can do it then i believe that i  can do it  supported by the you know the majority  of people in battle and spain  who just want to live together  peacefully send their kids to school  have a good nhs  look after their elderly relatives and  you know and and and just get on with  their lives and i think that's what we  all want to do now you know we've had  a lot of attention in battle and  spending the last few weeks indeed in  the last few years 