 disruptive you know and like i say  we've got a lovely selection of towns  and villages across batley and spain  where  where people just want to get on with  their lives and when the media descends  and when people from out of this area  descend  it is disruptive it's not good for  people so i'm really hoping that  we have a period of calm we have a  period of stability and and my role as  our mp will  will be pivotal in that but you know the  people around here are just amazing the  conversations i've had with people of  this  campaign have been so powerful and you  know i'm really looking forward to  working  together with them on what matters to  our towns and villagers  what did your parents say when or what  did the family say  when you said that you wanted to to run  uh  as an mp given what happened to joe in  such a tragic way when she was  representing the people of bethlehem  it was a big team decision it was a big  family decision  um but you know mum and dad have seen  the work that i've done through the  foundation  they've seen the network that i've got  across our local area  and how powerful that can be and a way  to build on that work  is by being our mp and they were very  very supportive of that and they always  said as well you know  if you don't do it you might regret not  going for it you know whatev whatever  happens  and yeah it was a team decision and  it's very emotional for us as a family  of course it is um  but listen if i can be half the mp that  joe was then i'll be very very happy and  very very proud of that  and will there be parts of joe that you  want to bring  to westminster do you i mean obviously  we know that you're  joe's sister you also want to be your  own person when you come to the palace  of westminster  but other uh characteristics of her that  you'll bring along with you for your  maiden speech for example  yeah i mean i'm kim ledbeter i am joe  cox's sister and that's how lots of  people know me and i've never been more  proud to be so but i  am doing this job very much as me one  thing i would say though is the way that  joe worked on a cross-party basis i  think is something which i always  admired and respected and i think  we don't do enough of that and we don't  talk enough about that you know the mps  that i've met and know  a lot of cross-party work goes on behind  the scenes but because it always isn't  as quite as controversial as  some of the other stuff it doesn't get  covered in the way that it maybe should  do  so i'll be looking to work on a  cross-party basis with  anybody who who is happy to do that on  the issues that matter to the people of  batley and spen  and the issues that matter more broadly  to the country okay  congratulations well done i know you've  got a lot to do today including uh being  congratulated  by the leader of the party try and get  some sleep at some stage but thanks for  talking to us  thanks for talking i will thank uk
 

